{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0186","billNumberShort":"S.B. 186","billNumberLong":"SB0186S02","fileNumber":"2026FL1064","shortTitle":"Charter School Modifications","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"BALDEH","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Balderree, Heidi","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"PIERUC","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Pierucci, Candice B.","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill establishes a charter school base funding study and creates a charter school educational service agency.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>requires a study of charter school administrative costs and funding options;<hr><ltbullet>establishes a charter school base funding study group with specific membership;<hr><ltbullet>requires charter school governing board members to take an oath of office;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies that charter schools are public schools;<hr><ltbullet>replaces the Charter School Revolving Account with the Charter School Revolving Fund; <hr><ltbullet>requires the study group to examine charter school administrative costs and funding options;<hr><ltbullet>directs the State Board of Education to report to the Legislature by December 1, 2026; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"","draftingAttorney":"Jeff Van Hulten","fiscalAnalyst":"Rachelle Gunderson","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/19/2026","trackingID":"RTTKBQQHPM","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-22 14:17:44.387","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-22 14:17:44.387","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceV